The AlphaBIOS firmware image file for LXs is called lx164nt.rom. Copy it
onto a FAT-formatted diskette. You can download it from ftp.digital.com
or I can email it to you. I have version 5.68-1 and it has no problem
with MILO. There are two ways to install the ROM image:
1) Insert the AlphaBIOS diskette & choose "Upgrade AlphaBIOS" from the
"AlphaBIOS Setup" menu.
2) Change the setting of jumper CF7, turn on the computer, wait until it
has beeped six times & the diskette drive light is off, insert the
diskette & press enter, choose "Upgrade AlphaBIOS" from the menu
like in method 1, then turn off the computer when it's done & set the
jumper back to its original setting.

