I have only recently got my AS 200 4/233 running linux so I cannot
provide much more than the sketchy details following (mostly because I
haven't figured out what happens yet).

For 6.1 I was never able to get the floppy installation to run correctly
and used the bootable 6.1 CD method using the following command:

boot dka0 -fi kernels/generic.gz -fl "root=/dev/scd0 text expert"

[for dka0 substitute your cdrom label]

and cancelling on the insert drivers at the beginning of the install.

Conversely on 5.2 I could only get a floppy install to work even though
I had an official RH 5.2 for Alpha CD. That command was:

boot dva0 -fi vmlinux.gz -fl "root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1
prompt_ramdisk=1"


Also, some instructions say not to touch the entire disk label 'c' on
the BSD fdisk step of the install, however do ensure that the type is
set to a BSD type (I used 4.1 BSD) from what was default 'unused' for
me.


Good luck,
Gord.


