    If you are installing clean on an SRM system, you can use the
    following instructions:

    Boot from the CD

>>>boot dqa0 -file "kernels/generic.gz" -flag "root=/dev/hda text"

Continue with the install till you have to partition the disks.
Control-F2 to another console
fdisk /tmp/sda
Type "b" to create a BSD disk label
Type "w" to write out the disk label
Type "q" to exit fdisk

Restart the system (press the reset button) and restart the
installation. Select one of the pre-packaged installs like
"KDE Workstation" or "Server". RH 6.1 will partition the
disk.

At the end of the installation, restart the system. At the SRM
prompt, type the following

>>> set boot_osflags 0
>>> set bootdef_dev dka0 (or whatever device you installed too)
>>> set boot_file ""

Now type "b" and hit return. The system will boot off the disk
and load the correct kernel called out in /etc/aboot.conf.

Enjoy,


mike


