"Mohan Vaghul" <mohan.vaghul@gte.net> writes:

> From you email, am to gather that I need only one image file - i.e. Xlt (or
> in case of 5.1, it is Xlt-alco) ? Does this image contain linload.exe? Or
> should I be renaming the Xlt-alco to linload.exe and then using rawrite to
> write to the floppy?
> 
> Mohan

There is no need to change the filename since nowhere does rawrite write the
name of the file onto the diskette; all rawrite does is write the contents of
the diskette image file directly onto the diskette, ingnoring any existing
data on the diskette, including filesystems. The diskette image file contains
a FAT filesystem with linload.exe in the filesystem's root directory.

