Yes, you should be able to boot directly off of the CD, that's what I
did because I also had problems with the kernel diskette. Type "boot
scd0:kernels/generic.gz root:/dev/scd0" (no quotes, replace scd0 with
whatever your CD drive is called) at the MILO prompt. If this doesn't
work, use "ls scd0:/" to see if there is a directory called something
like "kernels" (i.e. singular "kernel") or a kernel in the root
directory and to find out what the kernel's filename is.

