As I said elswewhere:
Quick method: Code s use an integer to keep track of the offset in
a file. A 32 bit system can't address more than 2^32 bytes offset.
In a 64 bit system, it can address 2^64. So, find yourself a great
big drive, and use cat to make a really huge file. Then use a code to
open it, lseek to the end, and tell you what is the final offset.

I just finished a sort on a 23 GByte file. Took forever, but it worked.






