amunk@efn.org wrote:
> (_Do not_ create the MILO partition from Disk Druid or
> Linux fdisk because AlphaBIOS can't see partitions that it didn't
> create itself.)

This part is trivially falsified by a simple experiment - at least on
all variants of ARC and AlphaBIOS which I have seen so far.

It is true that with a "virgin" disk it is a good idea to start with
making and formatting a small FAT partition from an AlphaBIOS menu.
One of reasons is that this will write some dummy "geometry" into
a partition table;  Linux will honour that and it will be not forced
to invent some on its own.  OTOH I can assure you that you can write
a partition table and format a FAT partition from Linux and AlphaBIOS
will be ok with that.  I did that many times.

  --mj

p.s. posting something with lines few hundred characters long is
not considered even half decent.



