In article <88etbh$n6t$1@nnrp1.deja.com>,
	timman <timftafischer@my-deja.com> writes:
> I did that.  During the kernel build the option is for ncr53c which
> covers 7xx and 8xx.  So why does it list as a 53c7 in /proc/scsi?????
If you're using "make config", you have to skip GENERIC.., etc.
This is from my .config file
# CONFIG_SCSI_GENERIC_NCR5380 is not set
# CONFIG_SCSI_NCR53C406A is not set
# CONFIG_SCSI_NCR53C7xx is not set
CONFIG_SCSI_NCR53C8XX=y
# CONFIG_SCSI_NCR53C8XX_NVRAM_DETECT is not set
CONFIG_SCSI_NCR53C8XX_TAGGED_QUEUE=y
CONFIG_SCSI_NCR53C8XX_IOMAPPED=y
CONFIG_SCSI_NCR53C8XX_MAX_TAGS=4
CONFIG_SCSI_NCR53C8XX_SYNC=10

This config works ok for the internal drive (until it crashed),
2 external drives and a tape drive.

Larry Z.




