I experienced a problem installing SuSE 6.3 on my Alpha XLT 300
(Alphabios).
After the installation program installed all packages on my harddrive it

crashed when it asked to reboot to commit the installation.
At this point the cursor remains blinking in the upper left corner of
the sreen.
The solution is to add 'fake_initrd' to your boot entry in your bios for
the floppy:

            boot fd0:/vmlinux.gz root=/dev/fd0 fake_initrd

With this the installation proceeds correctly and reboots with the
kernel from
your boot partitition on your harddrive.

Greetings,

Erik Louwman.




