bagnoli@dma.unifi.it wrote:
: When installing redhat 6.x on an au500 I got the following error:

: qlogicisp: new isp1020 revision ID (5) qlogicisp: i/o region
: 0x9000-0x90ff
: already in use ..

: scsi : 0 hosts found

: any suggestion?

Check axp-list archives on http://www.lib.uaa.alaska.edu/archives.html
Very recently somebody posted a solution for this.  Basically you
need another kernel with options where the region in question will
be not claimed and this one:

 ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/Linux-Alpha/Kernels/generic-up-2.2.12.gz 

is supposed to make it possible to boot with your controller.

Apparently Qlogic clashes with "Generic PCI IDE support" and
its "DMA support" options which will claim the same resources
so you have to turn that off in your kernel.

The above is the second hand information which I have no way to
verify myself.

  Michal




