> I am looking for suggestions regarding how to verify/prove that this
> particular installation is, in fact, running as a true 64 bit platform.
> 
> Any feedback will be greatly appreciated.


If my understanding is right, a 64bit operating system means 
that the address space it uses is 64bit long, i.e. it can 
support 2^64 bytes virtual address space. Linux/Alpha surely 
uses 64bit `void *' type, so it is a 64bit OS in this respect. 
Try the following program:

/**********************************************************************/
#include <limits.h>
#include <stdio.h>

int main(void)
{
    printf("size of pointer: %ld bits\n", sizeof(void *) * CHAR_BIT);
    return 0;
}

