Well, I'm a french Alpha reseller and we experienced most Linux/alpha
distributions, at least Red Hat, Debian and SuSE.
I'm not convinced that it's a good idea to offer Debian to someone who's looking
for a "user-friendly" distribution. Debian is totally GNU, with BSD initiation,
so it's probably the most interesting distribution for advanced and pro-GNU
users, but it is far less easy to install and configure for newbies than other
ditributions.
Personnaly, I chose the SuSE distribution. I found it the very easy to install
(especially the 6.3 which can directly boot from CD on most Alpha platforms),
far less buggy than Red Hat's and KDE runs well on it (for those who want
"user-friendly" interfaces).
I also believe that 1500 packages are enough for most users.
