This problem was solved by the following answer I received through
the SuSE list from Oleg Gusev <oleg@usm.uni-muenchen.de>

> Stock DIGIPAQ /usr/shlib/libc.so runs 'system()' with /usr/bin/sh or
> /sbin/sh. Do you have such binaries or links ? If not,
> system() will fail.

So, creating links from /bin/sh to /usr/bin/sh and to /sbin/sh solves
the problem.


However, I still can't run gv and/or ghostview using this trick: for
some reason the embedded gs interpreter produces a bus-error. Running
gs/gv/ghostview directly is not a problem at all. This is on SuSE 6.3.



