Are you sure that your nic is properly negotiating with your switch or hub.  This could be
a combination of srm settings, nic code switches and your hub or switch.  I have not used
your exact setup, but I have found the symptoms you descibe from the switch and nic being
at different settings (especially duplex).  If your hub or switch is manageable, you
should be seeing a lot of crc errors on the port you are plugged into.  If this is the
problem, you can look at the nic source and see how to hard set it to what you want and
then set your switch to match.
Good luck,
Chuck




