"Chris Csernica" <csernica@ihwy.com> wrote in message
news:38A3D1F2.9CD9A609@ihwy.com...
> Andrew Habgood wrote:
> >
> > Does anyone have a manual for the AS250?  Or a link to one.
>
> I've got one right here.
>
> > In particular, I need to know how to boot into the ARC console?
Currently
> > the machine boots straight into DEC UNIX, and I dont have the root pass
in
> > order to halt it.
>
> To change the console type, you need to get to the >>> prompt.
> Obviously, your system has the auto_action environment variable set to
> "boot".  Ctrl-C is supposed to halt the foreground process; I wonder if
> you can interrupt the boot process that way.  But suppose that doesn't
> work...
>
> <looking, looking....>
>
> OK.  Can you open up the box?  Look for J3 on the motherboard - It
> should be along the front edge of the motherboard around the center.
> It's probably shorting pins 1 and 2.  Try changing it to pins 2 & 3.
> This causes the reset button to issue a Halt Interrupt Request rather
> than a Reset.  You ought to be able then to halt the boot process as
> it's starting by pushing the reset button, and that should get you to
> the >>> prompt.
>
> Once you get there enter "set os_type nt".  Then cycle the power,
> leaving the machine off for at least 20 seconds.  According to the
> manual, you should be set.
>
> Sorry, but I'm not about to monkey with one of my company's machines to
> try this myself.  Good luck, though.
>
> -- Chris Csernica





