> Hi,
> Has somebody experinece with  XFree86 and Powerstorm 4DT60 graphics card
> on a linux-alpha system  (which is the appropriate X server and can it
> utilize all the  resource of the card)?
> 
> Regards,
> 
> Janos Lichtenberger

No support and nothing planned AFAIK. You can use the VGA channel of the
card. My current idea is to 

1. install a supported PCI graphics card (Matrox Millenium or S3 Virge)
in one of the PCI slots, 

2. disable the VGA on the 4D60T (jumper on the card), 

3. connect the Video-out from the new PCI card to the (black)
pass-through of the 4D60T.

This way I would be able to boot Digital/Unix (in VGA mode) and Linux
(in full X). If I had now an external switch to put the jumper on and
off the 4D60T I could use full X under both operating systems. Or maybe
it's possible to tell the Digital/Unix Xserver to use the VGA function
of the pass-through PCI card ... but I only found some Elsa Gloria
information in one of the configuration files.

Hope that helps

Clemens


