I had this problem when trying to upgrade the video card in my AS200.
The old video card would work fine, but a new video card would not.
After some investigation, I found that this was caused by old
firmware. The initialization of the video card is done by the
firmware, and if you have a video card that is newer or not recognized
by your current firmware, it will produce the situation that you
describe. I upgraded my firmware, and was then able to install almost
any card I wanted. Note that I still couldn't put any card I wanted
into the system, but I was able to get off the stupid 1MB video card I
was using and upgrade to a Millenium II.

Obviously you're going to have a little trouble setting up a new
firmware if you have no video, but if you use a serial terminal, I
think you can do it. Hope this helps.



