Hello everyone,

I've just successfully installed a CD burner into my SX164 and burned
my first audio disk with cdrdao. Trying to use xcdroast, I found that
cdwrite won't work because it asks the kernel for 4MB of shared memory
and the max size is defined to be slightly less. After changing the
#define in /include/asm-alpha/shmparam.h and recompiling the kernel,
it appears to work nicely, though.

My question is: can said change have any ill side effects? The system
is up and running, but I haven't done much with it yet. If changing
SHMMAX doesn't do any harm, then why is it lower on alpha than on
i386?

My System is: SX164, 128MB, NCR810 with 2 disks, CD burner, tape; 
