>     swriteboot /dev/sda bootlx vmlinux.gz
doing it this way writes the kernel immediately after aboot on the disk.

usually you just "swriteboot /dev/sda bootlx"  without the quotes, then pass
the kernel location either through the boot_file SRM logical or the "-fi"
flag on the command line.

Do a "man swriteboot"

fdisk defaults to look for FAT style partitions. type "m" at the fdisk
prompt and look at the options. I believe "b" switches it to bsd style
labels.

unfortunately, I do not have a running box at home right now... arggggg

JJ

