PseudoTensor wrote:
> 
> Dear all,
> 
> I'm a little confused.  Hardware component-wise, what's the diff between
> what people call ev6 and ev67?

The EV6 is the older proc, available up to 500 MHz in .35u techonolgy
EV67 is the 21264a, available at 750 MHz with 833 soon to come, made in
.25u

> Is it just the motherboard?  Or does it include the CPU?  Both?
> 
> eg.  I have a EV6 dual 21264 500Mhz system right now, purchased back in Aug
> 99.  Is it possible to upgrade to an "EV67 motherboard", getting the
> benefits of the EV67 arch?  Or does the CPU need to be EV67 too, whatever
> that means?

The dual EV6 is most probably a DP20. This has processors on
daughtercards, with 666 MHz just becoming available.
The other motherboard is the UP2000 with half the memory width (and
bandwidth) and with only one 64 bit PCI bus (the other is 32 bit) This
takes slot A processors with 750 MHz.

The UP2000 is smaller (fits in 3U rackmounts) and has the faster
processors available.
You DP20 has higher mem and PCI bw.

If you want to upgrade, you'll have to look for faster processor
daughtercards
- Alex



