How can you be sure? He did not tell his SCSI Ids.

>Since the 6.1 cd is bootable, try
>
>boot dka400 -fi /kernels/generic.gz -fl "root=/dev/scd0 expert text"
>
>The cd is either dka400 or dka500 do a "show device" at  the SRM console

The CD may be anything from dka000 to dka600 (if your host adapter is set to
7). 

Furthermore, I would guess that the above fails because the Jensen SRM is
limited to 8 characters of parameters for -fl - that was the reason why I
started enhancing aboot in the first place.

If the bootable CD has aboot on it,
boot dkaX00 -fl "i"
should get you to an aboot prompt, which enables you to choose a kernel and
pass a commandline of any length. IIRC, it should be something like

0/kernels/jensen.gz ro root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1

(with a kernel path/filename that is on the CD)

If that works, you should be able to boot from the CD and use the normal
installation path, and can forget about the tedious method using the
ARC-based minlabel/copyboot.

